(2) If the debtor agrees to the proposed variation of interest, the Certificate-holder shall, within thirty days of the service of the notice, file a Certificate of variation of the rate of interest in the office of the Certificate Officer.

(3) The Certificate of variation of the rate of interest shall be signed by the Certificate-holder and shall contain the following particulars, namely:-

(a) the original Certificate, the date on which it was filed and the number thereof;

(b) the Certificate-holder;

(c) the debtor;

(d) the original rate of interest;

(e) the proposed rate of interest;

(f) the date on which the notice was served on the debtor; and

(g) the date on which the Certificate of variation was filed.

